Subject: [PATCH] mesa: keep render-only multisample renderbuffers allocatable

Applies to Mesa 26.2.1, commit
da14d65e4499e66468094be52bff9ea0915a695e (third_party/mesa-pco.lock).

renderbuffer_alloc_storage chooses a renderable format/sample count, then
unconditionally adds PIPE_BIND_SAMPLER_VIEW. This fails on drivers whose
render-only sample count exceeds their texture sampling limit, e.g. a
16-sample renderbuffer with an 8-sample texture sampler limit.

Query the exact target, format, samples, storage samples and proposed
combined binding before adding that optional internal sampling capability.
Keep the required render/display/depth binding unchanged. Renderbuffer
limits and actual storage counts are not reduced or rounded differently.

Apply identically to both PvrGPU and llvmpipe Mesa source trees. This is
independent of the existing read-only MSAA ReadPixels resolve patch.

diff --git a/src/mesa/main/renderbuffer.c b/src/mesa/main/renderbuffer.c
--- a/src/mesa/main/renderbuffer.c
+++ b/src/mesa/main/renderbuffer.c
@@ -273,7 +273,12 @@ renderbuffer_alloc_storage(struct gl_context * ctx,
                     PIPE_BIND_RENDER_TARGET);
    }
 
-   templ.bind |= PIPE_BIND_SAMPLER_VIEW;
+   /* Sampling a renderbuffer is an optional internal optimization. Its
+    * supported render sample count can exceed the texture sampling limit. */
+   if (screen->is_format_supported(screen, templ.format, templ.target,
+                                   templ.nr_samples, templ.nr_storage_samples,
+                                   templ.bind | PIPE_BIND_SAMPLER_VIEW))
+      templ.bind |= PIPE_BIND_SAMPLER_VIEW;
 
    rb->texture = screen->resource_create(screen, &templ);
 
